  {"comment": "The transform tool's handles drive the active layer's live transform. A red stroke is painted on a layer named Paint and the tool opens with nothing selected (shot 1). The body is dragged and then the bottom right corner (shot 2), and Enter ends it as one step (shot 3). That step bakes the move and scale into Paint, an ordinary layer: the stroke is drawn moved and scaled, layers names Paint as untransformed, and texel reads the canvas under the old position as the ground. The tool opens again with its handles where the transform put the stroke (shot 4), the corner is dragged back (shot 5), and two undos show the stroke where it was painted (shot 6)."},
